doctors and other experts, and published studies in peer-reviewed journals. We believe you should always know the source of the information you're seeing. Learn more about our \u003ca href=\"/about-babycenter/company-information/babycenters-editorial-process-and-policies_10420233\"\u003eeditorial and medical review policies\u003c/a\u003e.","subtoutAppPromoOverrides":"{\"overrides\":[{\"contentAdTargeting\":\"babynames\",\"headline\":\"Swipe to find the perfect baby name, discover meanings, origins, and trends all in one place.\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2025/08/babyname-download-app-english-rejuv.svg\",\"ctaText\":\"Get the app\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://babycenter.onelink.me/nZLz/5k9vpcw2\",\"qrCodeSrc\":\"https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2025/09/babyname_qr_code.svg\"}]}","summaryHeading":"Quick summary","tableOfContents":{"tocHeader":"In this article","arrowAltText":"scroll down to item"},"testCommunityPostCarouselSlideshow":"{\"postLinkText\":\"Read the post\",\"active\":true,\"testData\":[{\"artifactId\":10408539,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"Anybody else having a hard time with the belly and finding a good position? I’m 33 weeks FTM and my husband is getting a little freaked out when the baby moves or just thinking that baby is “in the room with us” so he’s not feeling that comfortable with it. He’s still very attracted to me but when it actually comes down to it, it just feels off or like he gets turned off bc of the baby. I hope this doesn’t affect our relationship, especially since we won’t be able to do it after I give birth, so Idk what to do\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78645625/sex-positions\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"This all may be TMI Which sex position is good and comfortable? I have never been in this position before where sex has been uncomfortable... Help a girl out 😁\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78645302/sex-position\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"Is anyone else struggling with their sex life not being as enjoyable as it used to be? My last pregnancy, intimacy was great especially during the second trimester, but this time around its like the complete opposite and idk why. Without going into TMI details, it just feels like it's desensitized down there and I can never \\\"finish\\\". Does it get better after birth?\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78651330/sx-not-as-enjoyable\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":10355502,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"So my 3 month old has his first tooth! I couldn't believe it. I have 5 kids and this is the earliest I have ever seen one of my kids get a tooth! Anyone else's almost 4 month old getting teeth already? It seems so early!\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78646180/teething-already\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"My daughter is about to be 11 months old and she only has one tooth on the bottom. Is this normal? My older daughter had both her bottom and top teeth by a year old so idk if it is normal or should I be concerned 😭. Anybody else have an older baby with barely any teeth?\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78595853/baby-teething\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\" My 3 month old has been teething pretty bad. I was reading that orajel is no longer considered safe to give to babies, so instead we have been trying cold or frozen wash cloths for her to suck on and also camilla drops. It helps some, but shes still in so much pain. Looking for other suggestions of what I can try.\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78646594/teething\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":10414822,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"Team green but curious if anyone has any guesses based off of these pictures. Baby was crossing their legs almost the whole time :/\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78648797/just-for-fun-guess-the-gender\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"I want to know your thoughts on wife's tails about baby's gender. I know sometimes they are accurate but other times they are way off\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78646393/wifes-tails\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"Hello! Curious if anyone has any guesses on gender? This ultrasound is at 10 weeks 3 days, measuring 11 weeks. I did do one of those online tests that said girl based on skull theory. I know those aren’t always accurate, but what do you think and if you have done the online tests, were they accurate for you? I couldn’t see anything between the legs to see a nub during ultrasound, baby was super active and wiggly! Thanks!\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78645885/gender-prediction\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":5235305,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"My almost 6 month olds poop is pretty consistently green. He’s EBF \u0026 I’m used to the yellow seedy poop. Have any other EBF moms experienced this?\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78655231/ebf-baby-poop\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"My newborn never poops and it stresses me out! He’s two weeks old and besides the meconium poops at the beginning he’s only pooped maybe 4-5 times. Anyone else experiencing this? He’s formula-fed (Bobbie)\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78652130/newborn-poop\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"My breastfed daughter just had a blowout and I don’t think her poop looks normal. My doctor said he’s not concerned if it doesn’t have blood in it, but I just feel like something isn’t right. Is this indicative of MSPI? She is gassy, but she’s 8 weeks and I know it can be normal. Shes not really a fussy baby, just learning how to poop. Her bowel movements are the only thing that seem off to me right now.\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78653964/nsfw-bowel-movements\",\"commentCount\":3}]}]}","testCommunityPostCarouselArticle":"{\"postLinkText\":\"Read the post\",\"active\":true,\"testData\":[{\"artifactId\":10396237,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"What are you guys snacking on in between meals to keep the nausea at bay? My go-to is string cheese or a bowl of fruity pebbles 😂 I need to make more healthy decisions!\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78652375/snacky-snacks\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"So I am almost 13 weeks on saturday and I swear I'm always STARVING. I eat breakfast at 830 am and then by 1020 I'm just so hungry! Anyone else starving and not wanting to snack all day long! GIVE ME YOUR TIPS AND TRICKS!? My other pregnancies I was never this hungry all the time! WHY on the 5th pregnancy I have to be so HUNGRY! LOL\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78644133/always-hungry\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"Trying to stay healthy this pregnancy regardless of late night cravings 😂 what is your go to healthy snack? \\nOff the top of my head, I would say apples + feta cheese ! 🤤\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78645744/healthy-pregnancy-snacks\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":1313971,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"Anyone else struggling to eat healthy options? My nausea has been terrible. I'm currently 9 weeks 1 day and all I want is pizza and cheeseburgers 😩 Today for work I packed oatmeal, oranges, bananas, and triscuits with peanut butter for a snack. The thought of it made me want to puke. So I ordered a cheeseburger 🤦🏼‍♀️ I feel like I'm going to gain all my weight in the first trimester at this rate.\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78647984/junk-food-junky\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"Anyone had any weird cravings? I haven't had any \\\"weird\\\" cravings but sometimes I will get a craving for a certain food and there is nothing in the world that will stop me from having it. Last week I drove to 3 different stores to find coconut cashews. Yesterday I forced my husband to go to McDonald's just so I could have a Diet Coke fountain drink with light ice (Diet Coke from the bottle was NOT gonna do it). Today I planned on making chicken for dinner but decided a half hour before dinner that I wanted meatball subs with provolone. I cannot be the only pregnant woman that will go to the ends of the earth because of a craving!!\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78601988/weird-cravings-anyone\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"Just entered my six week and I'm starting to notice that food is everything…. Pregnancy craving banana peppers and pickles I don't like pickles or anything pickles. 1:23 AM I had to go on a massive Uber eats time to order pickles only to finally get it in bit into it and not even want it. It's gonna be a long journey. 🤣\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78653000/strong-cravings\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":41001726,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"Anyone have experience in this? Just heard about that theory. How it can catch it before pregnancy test. And I wanted to try it for fun. Got a super positive ovulation test. But negative pregnancy test. On day 10 after my ovulation. Day 24 of my 30 day cycle. Anyone have this happen and got a positive pregnancy test days later? I'm planning on testing pregnancy test again in another few days.\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78655595/ovulation-testing-for-pregnancy\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"I have been taking ovulation test today and yesterday at about the same time both days and the line has got darker i dont know if its postive or not? and I am supposed to get my period in two days and i took a pregnancy test yesterday it was negative. im so confused\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78653603/postive-or-no\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"\\t\\nHi everyone! I'm very new to all of this and I'm very curious how ovulation works as well as the test strips for it too! Lately I've been feeling very tired, very nauseous even while laying down and very bloated. I had my period for this month on the 7th already and I'm not sure when I should take a pregnancy test ? I don't have anyone to talk to that may honestly know more about it\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78651520/guidance\",\"commentCount\":3}]},{\"artifactId\":1508569,\"posts\":[{\"body\":\"Can you guys tell me your night and nap routines for your baby? Please give me every detail, I’m struggling with my daughter falling asleep. The only way I can get her to sleep is by baby wearing and aggressively walking around for naps, or nursing. but I’d like to transition away from that because I can never put her down without waking her. I’ve been tracking her wake windows and she usually has about 1.5 to 2 hours before getting fussy. Please tell me what has worked for you\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78654897/sleep-routine-help\",\"commentCount\":9},{\"body\":\"What are some good songs to sing to baby other than your typical lullaby. I've been singing \\\"Good morning Beautiful\\\",\\\"How Sweet it is\\\",\\\"Over the rainbow\\\"... looking to add more to my list\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78654128/baby-related-songs\",\"commentCount\":5},{\"body\":\"What are your babies bedtime routines like? I have a routine of getting my daughter into a clean diaper, read a few books and the last one is her prayers then I breastfeed, hold her up to burp and have to wait till she's fully asleep to put her in her bed or she cries and it breaks my heart so I pick her up. Pediatrician said she should be put down while still awake to fall asleep alone, I just don't have the stomach to do it when I know she just wants held. I have tried putting her down while she's drowsy and leaving the room for 3-5mins but once the real crying starts I go in to help soothe her. I feel like she will get to a point where she will want to go in bed alone even if not fully asleep. Am I delusional? 😓\",\"url\":\"https://community.babycenter.com/post/a78601394/bedtime-routine\",\"commentCount\":3}]}]}","timeline":{"titleBaby":"My baby month by month","newborn":"Newborn","months":"months"},"versionHistory":"Version History"},"offers":{"addressHeadingLine1":"To: You. From: Us.","addressHeadingLine2":"Time to Save Big","addressIntro":"Sign up to get freebies and great deals for mom \u0026 baby.","addressSubmit":"Get Freebies","carouselDisclosure":"We may earn commissions from these links.","carouselSeeMoreHeading":"Want to see more?","carouselSubtitle":"Enjoy the best handpicked deals \u0026 mama-approved offers.","carouselTitle":"Treat yourself – these deals are worth it!","dataSharing":"Data Sharing","emptyStateBody":"Looks like there aren’t any offers for you right now — but don’t worry, we’re always keeping an eye out for ones that are a perfect fit.","emptyStateTitle":"No Matches This Time, Mama","heading":"You Deserve the Best Hand-Picked Deals","loginHeading":"Log in to claim your exclusive offers.","metaDescription":"View your personalized offers","metaTitle":"Offers","noThanks":"No thanks, I don't want free stuff","redirectSuccessMessage":"~L  firepony.expert.offers.redirectSuccessMessage","refreshedOffersMessage":"Based on your stage, we've pulled together the top offers \u0026 deals for you right now.","registerHeading":"Sign up to claim your exclusive offers. It's free!","registerSubtext":"Need text here of some sort","subheading":"From freebies to discounts, here are some of the best pregnancy, baby, and parenting deals available now.","submit":"Submit","successMessage":"Congratulations! You’ve claimed the offer—enjoy!","seeAllOffers":"See all offers"}},"hostname":"www.babycenter.com","cookieHeaderBytes":null,"cookieTrimCandidates":null,"configs":{"facebookPageId":"6485616297","videoLazyLoadPxMob":1400,"videoLazyLoadPxDesk":800,"adRefetchInViewPercent":50,"adRefetchDurationTimer":30000,"adRefetchLimit":15,"adsRenderedThreshold":50,"snackbarAutoHideDuration":5000,"downloadAppDismissExpiration":432000000,"outOfPageAdMobileEnabled":true,"outOfPageAdDesktopEnabled":true,"urlPreviewOnPostsAndCommentsEnabled":true,"semRecaptch